  "summary": "A typical household photoelectric smoke detector: a 125 mm plastic disk about 25 mm thick. Air enters an optical chamber where an infrared LED and a photodiode sit at an angle. Smoke scatters light onto the photodiode and a piezo horn sounds. A 9-volt PP3 battery (48.5 mm by 26.5 mm by 17.5 mm) powers the board; a test button checks the horn.",
  "approximate": true,
  "disclaimer": "Researched typical design (125 mm disk, 25 mm thick, optical chamber, IR LED, photodiode, 9-volt PP3, piezo horn), not a specific product; simplified shapes.",
